      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $(x-1)^{2}+7{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2}\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+7(0)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}z & =\\pm (x-1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm 4(x-1).$",
